# What never belongs in the repository.
#
# The per-directory .gitignore files are a different job: storage/ has to exist
# in a clone and be empty, so each of its leaves carries a `*` plus
# `!.gitignore`. This file is about what the project produces, not about what it
# has to keep an empty place for.

# Secrets. .env.example is committed; .env never is.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output.
bin/
tmp/
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# `go build .` from the root drops the binary here, named after the module.
#
# It is NOT "/app". That rule was here while the entry point was ./cmd/app, and
# it silently excluded the whole app/ directory the day the tree became
# Laravel's -- every controller, model and policy, untracked and invisible.
/arandu

# Local module resolution while the framework is not published.
go.work
go.work.sum

# SQLite lives here in development. The file is never committed: the schema is
# database/migrations, and a committed database disagrees with them by the
# second day.
database/*.sqlite
database/*.sqlite-shm
database/*.sqlite-wal
database/*.db

# The compiled views.
#
# `aru view:build` writes home.go beside home.kyse.go, and Laravel does the same
# thing into storage/framework/views -- which it gitignores, for the reason this
# does: a compiled template is build output, and build output in a repository is
# a file people read diffs of, resolve conflicts in, and eventually edit.
#
# The build step is not optional and never was: `aru dev` runs it, the Taskfile
# runs it, CI runs it and the Dockerfile runs it. What changes is that the tree
# now shows what somebody wrote.
#
# A component LIBRARY is the opposite case and commits them: `go get` has no
# build step to run, so a module whose generated files are missing is one nobody
# can import. See arandu-io/kyse.
resources/views/**/*.go
!resources/views/**/*.kyse.go

# The Tailwind binary `aru view:build` downloads and pins. It is a tool, not a
# dependency: arandu.toml records which version, and that is what is committed.
.arandu/

# What the editors and the operating systems leave behind.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/

# .vscode IS committed, deliberately: it is what hides the generated views from
# the file tree, and a project where half the team sees them and half does not
# is a project arguing about a file nobody edits.
!.vscode/
